## Core concept:
I want to create a product around lawyers, which has a set of master data holding templates and it can be filled based on template type.  
 
Let's say I have a template to send a Legal Notice. There are some variables holding those and some are stored in memory. Help me in designing & developing whole level architecture and fabulious UI / UX that user actually likes it.

## User UI:
1. The whole screen will resemble MS Word doc screen, for reference `docs/business-docs/MSWord-screenshot.png`.
2. There is "Office Addin React App" loaded on left side of the user doc.

## User Actions:

### Journey 1 (New template drafting):

#### Journey 1.1:
1. User can create a new template with label as "Create a new template", description like "Turn your current document into a standard template".
2. Then user is able to Enter name of the template (text type), Select Template Type, Select template sub type, and add a note or description.
3. There is a CTA provided "Auto Detect Variables" to identify variables from the doc, on click we will call AI LLM.
4. We will pass content to AI and see if AI is able to process the document and able to identify alteast 80% variables.
5. We will provide Information about the variable identification. These many variables are identified.
6. Then we will process the template having variable's with name. [variable name]
7. Below the CTA we will ask user to confirm variable detection and custom added variables are correct. Checkbox with text as "I confirm the detected and custom added variables".
8. Below that we have two CTA's side by side, "Create Template" & "Choose Existing Template".
9. If he clicks on "Create Template", we will save variables against the template name in Database. See "Journey 1.2" for further catch up.
10. If user selects "Choose Existing Template" then go to "Journey 1.3".

#### Journey 1.2:
1. User first selects "Template type" from a searchable select bar.
2. There is a CTA provided to identify variables from the doc, on click we will call AI LLM to identify if any new variables are to be identified.
3. We will pass content to AI and see if AI is able to process the document and able to identify alteast 80% variables.
4. We will provide Information about the new variable identification. These many variables are identified.
5. Then we will process the template having variable's with name. [variable name]
6. Below the CTA we will give checkbox to "Update the Master Template".
7. If user checks the checkbox we will append new variables with old ones, against the template name in Database.
 
#### Journey 1.3:
1. After the user clicks on "Create Template" (Journey 1.1) or clicks "Fill the form" (Journey 1.2) CTA a new screen will open.
2. On that screen we have all the dynamic variables, the form has all text inputs, user entered those values with validation checks.
3. Once user enters all the values he can click on "Apply Data".
4. Open the preview in the docs & edit if user wants.
5. Save each and every variable in database.

## Expectations:
1. Focus on drafting thing only, nothing else.
2. User friendly editing screens and variable injection in template after form/table is filled.